<title>PERU: Peru's July wheat production rises 25.1 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's July wheat production rises 25.1 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's July wheat production rose 25.1 percent to 46,232 tonnes, compared to the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Output for the first seven months was up 33 percent to 109,039 tonnes, compared to the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Total 1995 wheat production was 125,048 tonnes.</p>
<p>Wheat imports in July rose 39.7 percent to 116,119 tonnes, worth $27.132 million, while in the first seven months imports rose 0.7 percent to 634,029 tonnes, worth $136.336 million.</p>
<p>Peru's wheat is grown mostly in the central and southeastern Andean regions.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
